  "title": "CAS500-2 & CAS500-4 launch May 3 on Falcon 9 — Korea EO satellites",
  "url": "https://nextspaceflight.com/launches/details/8213/",
  "snippet": "South Korea's CAS500-2 and CAS500-4 Earth observation satellites are scheduled for launch on May 3, 2026 aboard a SpaceX Falcon 9 from Vandenberg Space Force Base. CAS500-2 provides 0.5m panchromatic / 2m multispectral high-resolution imagery. CAS500-4 carries a wide-area EO camera with 5m resolution and 120km swath width, optimized for agriculture, forestry, and land-use monitoring. Both satellites enter Sun-synchronous orbits operated by KARI.",
